+verdict: don't merge
+issue_repro: fail
+branch_tests: pass
+test_checks_the_fix: no
+
+Why: the branch joins quoted lines, so the fixture gives 3 rows, but it leaves the
+CRLF carriage returns in place, so strip('"') never removes closing quotes. The
+issue's repro returns note 'call back\r\nafter 5pm"\r', not 'call back\r\nafter
+5pm'; the header and first row also keep trailing \r and/or a quote.
+
+The odd-quote-count heuristic adds silent data loss: one stray quote in an
+unquoted field ('1,5" pipe,x') discards the rest of the file, and a file ending
+inside a quoted field returns no rows at all rather than erroring.
+
+The new test only exercises bare LF input, and its second assertion codifies a
+separate bug (a quoted comma splits into two fields). It therefore passes while
+the reported Windows-line-ending case is still parsed wrongly.
